  },
  "description": "ATOPAC crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P 21 21 21. Reported CIF formula moiety: C83 H124 Co2 Gd3 N1 O29 P2,C5 H10 O2,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Co1 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.533-4.123 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.69-119.26°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Co2Gd3(OH)(RPO3)2(tBuCO2)8(tBuCO2H)2(py)(H2O)2]·2H2O·tBuCO2H (R = 9-methyl-9H-fluoren-9-yl). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
